<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech bank CSOB CZK 3.01 bln 96 net profit - IAS.</title>
<headline>Czech bank CSOB CZK 3.01 bln 96 net profit - IAS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results, calculated according to international accounting standards (IAS) for year ending December 31, 1996: (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit	     3.006	vs	2.85</p>
<p> Pre-tax profits	3.022	vs	3.119</p>
<p> Operating Income     8.611	vs     10.099</p>
<p> Non-interest income  4.217	vs	4.404</p>
<p>Net commission</p>
<p>  income		  1.417	vs	1.573</p>
<p> Net interest income  4.394	vs	5.695</p>
<p>Amount owed</p>
<p>  to banks	     59.331	vs     53.372</p>
<p>Amount owed to</p>
<p>  customers	    90.632	vs     83.376</p>
<p> Total liabilities  189.142	vs    173.522</p>
<p>Loans and advances</p>
<p>  to banks	     50.224	vs     48.191</p>
<p>Loans and advances</p>
<p>  to customers	 86.506	vs     80.915</p>
<p> Debt securities     12.300	vs     12.573</p>
<p> Treasury bills	19.310	vs     18.294</p>
<p> Total assets	 206.689	vs    190.248</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Ceskoslovenska Obchodni Banka a.s.. The bank is wholly-owned by Czech and Slovak government agencies. Results are consolidated.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
